1
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,837
The world, what a glorious place.

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:16,077
Seek freedom, and it will lie
stretched out before your eyes.

3
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:19,340
If the endless dream guides
your restless spirit,

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,980
seize it, raise your flag and stand tall.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,717
I think back to the time
when my search first began.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,337
I left behind those shores of sand.

7
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:38,700
For the endless everlasting
world out there.

8
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,817
I know that with this
burning passion driving me.

9
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,540
Someday, somewhere, I'll finally see the
light I have searched for everywhere?

10
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,757
When the summer sun is shining.

11
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,620
Shaking the sails of my heart. I know.

12
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:05,817
A brand new world that has been hiding.

13
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,917
Has opened up its doors for me to go.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,900
A way from the moon's sky.

15
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:15,377
Wearing in the troubled waves.

16
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:17,877
From all despair I can be saved.

17
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:21,177
For the horizon on the other side is.

18
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,497
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

19
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,577
Is what I am for?

20
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:28,660
And though I travel far
from where my search began,

21
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,280
over seas of green and shores of sand,

22
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:34,560
through the endless
everlasting world out there.

23
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:38,780
I know that with this
burning passion driving me,

24
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:44,260
someday somewhere I'll finally see the
light I will search for everywhere.

25
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,457
Where the heck is that
rubbery, bug-eyed idiot?

26
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:58,900
This is just like him.

27
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:01,837
Didn't we all agree to be
here over 45 minutes ago?

28
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,626
We're gonna miss the current.

29
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:08,517
I'm sure the genius didn't even stop to
consider how the gold would weigh him down.

30
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,797
Why does he always insist on
making everything ten times harder?

31
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:14,980
The only schedule Luffy's
concerned with is his own.

32
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:17,017
Yeah, he's got a point there.

33
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,557
You don't think someone in
town beat him up, do you?

34
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,317
What, you mean that guy Bellamy?

35
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,837
Well, if Bellamy didn't beat him
up, you better believe I will!

36
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,744
Oh, was that right, tough girl?

37
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,250
Hey!

38
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,030
Huh?

39
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,040
Look there! He's back!

40
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,077
I knew he'd make it!

41
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,360
I did it, you guys!

42
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:45,268
Luffy, hurry, we're
already behind schedule.

43
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,360
Look, it's a Hercules!

44
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,357
It took me forever to find it!

45
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,620
You're kidding me!

46
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:53,840
Are you crazy?

47
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,640
Whoa, that's awesome!

48
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:07,869
Introducing the Going
Merry Flying Edition.

49
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:09,000
It can fly?

50
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,470
Why?!

51
00:03:10,553 --> 00:03:11,383
I know!

52
00:03:11,466 --> 00:03:13,000
They built it just for us!

53
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:18,970
Morons.

54
00:03:19,053 --> 00:03:21,446
Something about it makes
me feel kinda uneasy.

55
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,197
Well, for once I agree with you.

56
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,137
Chickens don't even know how to fly.

57
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,877
They should've made it a pigeon.

58
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,677
What's that got to do
with anything, you dope?!

59
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:31,360
It's time to set sail!

60
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,417
Come on, if you're with
me, let me hear it!

61
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,330
Yeah!

62
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,591
What are you waiting for?

63
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:46,600
Get on board, unless you plan on missing
your chance at the sky, like a fool.

64
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,060
Thanks for the ship.

65
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,720
Thank them.

66
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,100
They built it.

67
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:58,680
Yeah, thanks for the ship, you guys.

68
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,640
You can have my Hercules.

69
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,080
Ooh, really?

70
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,280
You mean it?

71
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,460
Are you sure?

72
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:07,357
That's so kind of you.

73
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:09,960
All right, enough of this foolishness!

74
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:12,240
We don't have much time! Follow us!

75
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:13,780
We'll lead the way!

76
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,640
Come on, Luffy, let's go! Coming!

77
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:27,080
This city of gold is just a fairy
tale that Lion Nolan dreamt it all up!

78
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,350
Saruyama!

79
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:32,790
Aye!

80
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,417
I'm counting on you men.

81
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,217
I don't care what happens.

82
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:41,597
You give our friends here
everything you've got.

83
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:48,020
Time to set sail!

84
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,917
You heard him, shove off! Alright!

85
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,720
Yes, Nabi.

86
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:11,420
Well, kid, looks like this
is where we part ways.

87
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:13,650
Yep.

88
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:18,760
There's only one thing you gotta
remember above everything else. What?

89
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:25,580
Not one person in history has ever
disproved the existence of Sky Island.

90
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,270
Hmm.

91
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:31,625
People may say I'm crazy and even
laugh at me, but I don't care.

92
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:37,220
I'm a romantic like you romantic

93
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,360
So long

94
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:48,220
Oh yeah thanks for the gold

95
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:52,760
And hey don't be falling
from the sky you hear

96
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:59,520
See you around pops thanks
for everything cricket?

97
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:03,596
Think of us when you find
the City of Gold, old-timer!

98
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,100
Try and take it easy, okay?

99
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,580
Mind your own business.

100
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,540
It's morning already?

101
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:22,780
Burgess, see anything out there?

102
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:26,349
Can't even see an
outline of the shore yet.

103
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,821
You really think they're
going to that Sky Island?

104
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:30,770
Yeah,

105
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:34,057
so they say they'll be pretty
tough to follow up there,

106
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,611
so we gotta take care of them before that.

107
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,480
Okay, listen up!

108
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,680
It's currently 7 a .m.

109
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:44,540
We need to arrive at our final
destination no later than 11.

110
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,757
It's like Cricket already told us.

111
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:51,360
The spot where the knock-up stream
erupts is different every single time.

112
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:56,564
We need to get there as early as possible
in order to pinpoint its exact location.

113
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,020
Check it out!

114
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:02,457
It looks like we're already
running a little behind schedule.

115
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:05,080
Hey, are you knuckleheads
paying attention?

116
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,800
Did you see that?

117
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:09,520
It has to face forward.

118
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:12,076
I've never seen a bird quite like it.

119
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,760
He only faces south. Isn't that funny?

120
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,353
The goofy bird acts just like a compass.

121
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,577
Did you hear what it said?

122
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,677
He said he's going to
face a different direction

123
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:27,289
on purpose and laugh
at us once we're lost.

124
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,240
Go ahead and try.

125
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,480
Whoa, he's really facing north.

126
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,700
Told ya he couldn't do it.

127
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:50,300
Hey, show the boss some respect
and pipe down over there.

128
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,440
Nah, they're fine. Why?

129
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:56,817
It reminds me of the old days
when I was young and irreverent.

130
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:57,860
Uh-oh.

131
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,340
They say...

132
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,710
Hey!

133
00:08:00,793 --> 00:08:03,287
There's no point getting
so worked up, Fall!

134
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,080
Try to relax!

135
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,736
And who put us behind schedule again?

136
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,030
You know what?

137
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:09,943
He's right.

138
00:08:10,026 --> 00:08:11,597
Being tense won't get us anywhere.

139
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,497
We may as well enjoy ourselves.

140
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,840
I see your point.

141
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:16,354
Full speed ahead, men!

142
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,600
Anyone not relaxing answers to me!

143
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:23,940
That's better.

144
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,020
This is ridiculous.

145
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,880
Boss, look!

146
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,320
What's wrong?

147
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:34,620
I see the Kimulo Regalis
Cloud to the southwest!

148
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,110
It can't be!

149
00:08:36,193 --> 00:08:37,023
What time is it?

150
00:08:37,106 --> 00:08:37,936
Ten o 'clock!

151
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,920
They're a full hour early!

152
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,800
Shoujo, do you think we can make it?

153
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,880
Dispatch the Udon divers!

154
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,693
Find me those currents!

155
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,400
They're incredible!

156
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,740
What's going on now?

157
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:58,517
The cumuloregalus clouds appeared
a lot sooner than expected,

158
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:01,365
so now everyone's scrambling
to find a current!

159
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,715
Sonar waves detected!

160
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,057
There's a large current at 12 o 'clock!

161
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:14,097
Large creature detected at 9 o 'clock!

162
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,474
It could be a sinking!

163
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:20,637
There's wave activity detected at 10
o 'clock going against the current!

164
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,477
I believe it's a giant whirlpool, sir!

165
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,740
That's it!

166
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:26,097
Full speed ahead directly for 10 o 'clock!

167
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:29,097
That's where the knock-up stream's
gonna erupt, I'm sure of it!

168
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:30,010
Now go!

169
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:35,530
Hold on!

170
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,506
The waves are getting higher!

171
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:38,880
We're gonna sink!

172
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,320
Steady, men!

173
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:45,240
It's a pre-eruption tremor! Eruption?

174
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,120
Hey, Navigator!

175
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:49,100
What has the log post said?

176
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:57,877
It's pointing straight at those clouds
you mean the sky islands above that the

177
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:01,797
wind direction's perfect the clouds are
lining up exactly over the center of the

178
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:08,277
whirlpool what whirlpool i haven't seen
anything nice work brother i think we

179
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:13,007
hit the jackpot this time yes and it
seems we're in for a nice-sized explosion.

180
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,837
Do you think we'll make it?

181
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:15,760
Of course.

182
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,630
What's that?

183
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:21,140
We'll lead you to the inner edge.

184
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:23,481
All right, but what should we do?

185
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:26,897
Position yourself on the floor
and head towards the center.

186
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,156
Then you'll be fine.

187
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:31,022
He wants us to go to the center?

188
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:39,357
I don't remember signing up
for all this. Don't worry.

189
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,617
I'll make sure nothing happens to you.

190
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:44,171
I've never seen one quite this big before.

191
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,957
This is bad! I changed my mind!

192
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,097
I want to go back!

193
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:52,240
Sorry, Usopp. Too late for that.

194
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:54,262
You know who is already excited.

195
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,240
Let's go to the sky!

196
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,760
It's time for us to go.

197
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:24,300
The rest is up to you now. Good luck.

198
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:27,509
Bye, guys, and thanks
a lot for everything!

199
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:29,120
Don't go! Don't go!

200
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:30,436
I don't want to die!

201
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,112
Please take me with you!

202
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,140
Give me a break, I'm scared!

203
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:35,720
Please don't make me!

204
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:40,237
No one said anything about diving
headfirst It's into a giant whirlpool!

205
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,060
It's getting dark! Oh no!

206
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,520
I think so did!

207
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,177
That would be so unreasonable, Luffy!

208
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,897
Let's go back while we still have time!

209
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:51,097
Don't you understand the Sky Island
stuff is just a bunch of make-believe?

210
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,121
It's not worth getting us killed!

211
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,900
It's all make-believe?

212
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,360
Is that what you think? Usopp's right!

213
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,600
I think this is a really bad idea!

214
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:02,680
It may be a stupid
dream, but I have to try!

215
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,699
It could be our greatest adventure!

216
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:07,290
No!

217
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:08,636
Well, it's too late!

218
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:16,557
Instead of wasting your time bickering,
you all might want to take a look.

219
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,640
What do you mean?

220
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:21,960
It's sucking us in.

221
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,740
Hurry, Nami, let my arms look at you!

222
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:37,750
What happened?

223
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:38,663
It disappeared.

224
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:39,860
What's going on?

225
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,940
Wait, I don't get it.

226
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,240
Where'd it go?

227
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:51,470
I feel it.

228
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,690
It's starting.

229
00:12:56,300 --> 00:12:58,476
The whirlpool sunk under the surface.

230
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:02,922
You don't mean.

231
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,260
Hold it right there.

232
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:09,820
Hey, Zoro. Huh?

233
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:11,250
Look.

234
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:20,420
Well, well, well.

235
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,240
If it isn't straw and loopy.

236
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,820
It's him.

237
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,393
It's that Mocktown guy.

238
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:28,960
What guy?

239
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:32,977
I've come all this way to collect
on your 100 million fairy bounty.

240
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:34,100
So don't be shy.

241
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:41,747
Were those youngsters
expecting some company?

242
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,440
I don't know, brother.

243
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:48,950
Huh?

244
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:50,842
Why is it getting dark out here?

245
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:51,960
100 million?

246
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,937
What are you talking about?

247
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,840
Don't play dumb with me, kid.

248
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,920
It says right here, Monkey D.

249
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:00,766
Luffy won it for 100 million.

250
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:05,737
And for Pirate Hunter
Zoro, 60 million Barry.

251
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:06,940
It's true.

252
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:09,297
He's got a different
poster for each of you.

253
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:12,086
Hey, Zoro, congratulations
on your new bounty.

254
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,620
Wait a minute, Usa.

255
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:14,820
Come on.

256
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,334
Do you see one for me?

257
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:18,010
Uh, no.

258
00:14:18,093 --> 00:14:18,960
Look closer.

259
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:20,670
Nothing.

260
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:26,757
It looks like your bounties must have
gone way up after the Alabasta incident.

261
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,134
But a hundred million?

262
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,920
This is great! Hear that?

263
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,480
My bounty went up big time!

264
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,453
Ha, ha, 60 million's not too bad either.

265
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,180
It's not a good thing!

